// ============================================================
//  What belongs in this file, and what does not
//
//  mn_rules now handles vowel harmony, unstable-vowel deletion,
//  the aspiration series, palatalisation, and the г/х/л allophones.
//  Several hundred ordinary words that used to be listed here were
//  only compensating for rules that could not do that yet, and have
//  been removed: the rules derive them correctly, and a stale copy
//  in this file would silently override any future rule fix.
//
//  Four things still have to be listed, because no letter-to-sound
//  rule can derive them:
//
//    1. Number and symbol names, which are spoken forms of digits
//       and punctuation, not spellings.
//    2. Clitics and particles, which need prosodic flags ($u,
//       $pause) rather than a different pronunciation.
//    3. Loanwords, which do NOT undergo unstable-vowel deletion.
//       редактор is [retakʰtʰɔr]; the native rules would reduce its
//       final о to a schwa.
//    4. Abbreviations, whose spoken form is a convention, not a
//       reading of the letters.
//
//  Phoneme symbols follow ph_mongolian: p t k are UNASPIRATED
//  (б д г), ph th kh are aspirated (п т к), ts/tsh are з/ц,
//  tS/tSh are ж/ч, l# is [ɬ], q is uvular [ɢ], X is uvular [χ].
// ============================================================


