// ============================================================
//  Ordinals written as a digit + hyphen + р
// ============================================================
//  5-р сар is May, 3-р хороо is the 3rd district. Without these the digit and
//  the р are read separately: 10-р сар came out аравр сар.
//
//  numbers.c reconstructs the suffix across the word break -- it prepends the
//  hyphen when FLAG_HYPHEN_AFTER is set and reads the following word -- so a
//  `_#-<suffix>` entry is all that is needed. Crimean Tatar does the same for
//  its N-nci ordinals, and Hungarian and Esperanto also use hyphenated `_#-`.
//
//  The split follows the orthography: `_#-р` is the letter that is actually
//  written, and each `_No` carries the cardinal plus the harmonising -дугаа
//  (RTR) or -дүгээ (ATR). So 10-р = аравдугаа + р.
//
//  Composition ordinalises only the FINAL element, which is Mongolian's rule
//  too: 21-р is хорин нэгдүгээр, so only _1o is consulted for the units.

_#-р    r
// Roman numerals reach the same ordinal forms by a different route:
// TranslateRoman rebuilds the number as "21 <roman_suffix>" with a SPACE, so the
// suffix arrives without the hyphen and needs its own entry. Same value.
_#р     r

