// ============================================================
//  Personal-name initials
// ============================================================
//  "Д. Нацагдорж" is the conventional way to write a Mongolian name, and
//  the initial was coming out as a bare vowelless consonant -- a lone [t],
//  which is not audible as anything. A single letter only spells itself
//  when the letter-to-phoneme rules produce NOTHING (translateword.c), and
//  every Cyrillic letter produces something, so the spelling path was never
//  reached. (Ч. appeared to work only by coincidence: `ч` is also the
//  clitic "too", listed above as tShi, which happens to resemble a letter
//  name. Its real name is tShe.)
//
//  $hasdot + $capital fire only on an upper-case letter followed by a dot,
//  which is a name initial and nothing else. Running text is untouched: the
